  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Sam wanted to estimate the rate of weight growth of his new puppy. He took note of its weight every week, for $7$ weeks. The results are shown in the table below, where $W(t)$ is the puppy's weight (measured in pounds) after $t$ weeks from birth.\n\n| **$t$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $W(t)$ | $9$ | $10.1$ | $11.3$ | $12.4$ | $13.5$ | $14.6$ | $15.8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the puppy's rate of weight growth $12$ weeks after birth using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$",
